completed qualification, then its evidence carrier refused the maintenance workflow ref. Add only the exact named maintenance branch and constrain maintenance release carriers to stable 4.44 versions. Preserve all source, workflow, job, event, run-attempt and inventory checks.\n\nValidation: all 16 carrier tests and 15 source-gate controls passed; exact commit message and locked dependency signatures passed. The original failed [push run](https://github.com/Hexalith/Hexalith.Builds/actions/runs/44121371373) remains failed. Fresh PR and merged-source CI are required before publication.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes release qualification gatekeeping for a maintenance branch; mistakes could block legitimate 4.44 releases or accept wrong versions, but scope is narrow and heavily tested.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Qualification evidence archiving was rejecting producer runs from the **`4.44.x`** maintenance branch even though CI already runs there. The allowed `GITHUB_WORKFLOW_REF` pattern now includes **`heads/4.44.x`** alongside `main`, `prerelease`, and PR merge refs.\n> \n> For **release** carriers triggered from that branch, inventory **`version`** must be an exact stable **`4.44.*`** (no pre-releases or other major lines); otherwise archiving fails with a clear error.\n> \n> New contract tests cover successful CI/release binding on `4.44.x`, rejection of near-miss refs/tags and invalid versions, and confirm existing producer-identity checks still apply on the maintenance path.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 4a7e0d22e79aeb26f73fd4b147cd4edece8e4f26. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-17T16:26:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T16:27:56Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"50f60